# Paths where an unreviewed change is a security change.
#
# Write access to a workflow is write access to deployment credentials: a
# workflow can print an OIDC-issued session, or add a step that assumes the
# deploy role and does anything that role can do. The same is true of the
# CloudFormation templates that define the role, and of the scripts CI invokes.
# These paths therefore require a review from an owner before merge.
#
# This file is only enforced when branch protection on `main` has "Require review
# from Code Owners" enabled. scripts/guardrails-check.sh asserts that this file
# exists and covers the paths below; it reports branch protection separately,
# because CODEOWNERS without it is a suggestion.
#
# A fork must replace @vppillai with its own owner or team. Ownership cannot be
# derived: GitHub resolves these handles against this repository's collaborators.

# Everything, by default. Later rules win, so this is the floor and not the ceiling.
*                       @vppillai

# CI: holds the deploy credentials.
/.github/workflows/     @vppillai
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @vppillai

# Infrastructure: defines the deploy role, the permissions boundary, the deny
# policies and every data store.
/infrastructure/        @vppillai

# Operations scripts: bootstrap-agent.sh creates the agent principal, deploy.sh is
# the only path to a deployed stack, teardown.sh and cleanup-aws.sh delete data.
/scripts/               @vppillai

# Instance configs drive the deployment matrix — adding a file here deploys a
# stack.
/config/instances/      @vppillai
